shape theory.dimension.chirality : theory.dimension.generator {
  type: definition
  layer: 0
  """
// Definition 8.3 (Chiral Generator).
// A chiral generator is a closed loop through the transformation
// structure that traverses two or more spatial generators.
// In N spatial dimensions, the set of such closed paths traces the
// N-dimensional unit sphere.
//
// 2D: circle (S^1). 3D: sphere (S^2). 4D: 3-sphere (S^3).
// The sphere is itself a shape.
//
// Definition 8.5 (Chiral Commitment).
// The chiral commitment of a shape is the structure committed to
// maintaining its chiral loop. This is the structural investment
// required to sustain multi-step closure through the chiral generators.
//
// Theorem 8.4 (Internal Dimensionality).
// A shape system defined by N generators has internal dimensionality
// 2N: N spatial generators and N chiral generators.
// (N-1 angular degrees of freedom on the chiral sphere + 1 magnitude
// of chiral commitment = N chiral degrees, independent of N spatial.)
//
// Chirality is structurally forced at N >= 2.
//
// Derives from: theory.dimension.generator
  """
}
